Adopted from Alexander Theissen's (athei) Wine tree, commit a4e40c6bf867708d43c1c1a8c6be7ec3e81af190
("ntdll: HACK: Recognize ROSETTA_X87_PATH and attach x87sidecar cooperatively.", github.com/athei/wine,
LGPL-2.1-or-later), as carried by highball-engine (https://github.com/gauthierpiarrette/highball-engine,
LGPL-2.1-or-later) in patches/0012-ntdll-x87sidecar-cooperative-attach.patch at commit
a2b10db8b86f4ed5f02855a41fa7c6ad4d3cbfb6. Only the get_alternate_wineloader() hunk is taken, its lines
unchanged; the x87sidecar parts (coop_proto.h, the handshake, the preloader_exec change) are not.

ntdll: Return no alternate loader when it does not exist.

This engine is wow64-only: lib/wine has i386-windows, x86_64-unix and x86_64-windows, and no
i386-unix. get_alternate_wineloader() still names lib/wine/i386-unix/wine for a 32-bit image, and
build_initial_params() in env.c takes any non-NULL answer as a reason to relaunch the program through
start.exe /exec. So every 32-bit program started from the Mac side ran as a second Wine process, a
child of start.exe, with launchd as its Unix parent, inside start.exe's job, with its command line
rebuilt by start.exe. Measured on revision 1 of this engine: syswow64\notepad.exe ran as two
processes ("start.exe /exec" plus the program, parent pid 1); with WINEARCH=wow64, which makes the
same function return NULL, it ran as one. With this check an unset or win64 WINEARCH behaves the same
way. 64-bit programs never reach the check. An engine that does ship an i386-unix loader keeps
today's behaviour.

Upstream status: not in Wine (master eba89375, 2026-10-05) or CrossOver 26.3.0. A note offering it
upstream is drafted in patches/upstream/0004-ntdll-no-alternate-loader-when-missing.md; not sent yet.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -524,6 +524,17 @@
     else if (alt_build_dir)
         asprintf( &ret, "%s/loader/wine", alt_build_dir );
 
+    /* Installations without a 32-bit Unix loader (wow64-only builds) have no
+     * i386-unix directory, so the constructed path may not exist. Callers
+     * treat a non-NULL return as proof that another loader must run the
+     * image: loader_exec execs it and env.c falls back to start.exe, which
+     * relaunches the main exe in a detached process. Verify the loader is
+     * actually there so those callers behave as if WINEARCH=wow64 was set. */
+    if (ret && access( ret, X_OK ))
+    {
+        free( ret );
+        ret = NULL;
+    }
     return ret;
 }
 
